                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b4b8d36c-ad08-4de6-b0bd-86b2f96b56ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "38f053e3-9424-36e2-bc18-0f1a8f6d908c",
                        "target_lang_word": "ideell",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ideell",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1424f937-4457-315e-8300-43fff9bec244",
                                        "entry_id": "db955a22-fdf7-3d7e-a4d2-5df69e27e13a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nur in Gedanken existierend; nur gedanklich"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a655aad5-0a33-4b81-9e4f-c0ef8ee95dfb",
                                                "sense_id": "1424f937-4457-315e-8300-43fff9bec244",
                                                "text": "„In dieser Situation bieten fundamentalistische Bewegungen nicht nur materiell ein Netz sozialer Sicherheit, sondern auch ideell Vorstellungen einer alternativen sozialen Ordnung an […].“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43fe0f9d-fe3e-4343-b8eb-887216f2e3c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "38f053e3-9424-36e2-bc18-0f1a8f6d908c",
                        "target_lang_word": "ideal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ideal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0cbd1d0-4251-3151-a8a1-44f994cc4cee",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to ideas, or to a given idea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db4a3c32-86ce-356f-9d1b-97a747b920c4",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Existing only in the mind; conceptual, imaginary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6640f52a-22d2-4de8-b361-ba190670b469",
                                                "sense_id": "db4a3c32-86ce-356f-9d1b-97a747b920c4",
                                                "text": "The idea of ghosts is ridiculous in the extreme; and if you continue to be swayed by ideal terrors —"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49a1e40f-f406-447a-b8a1-da1aa9c362ae",
                                                "sense_id": "db4a3c32-86ce-356f-9d1b-97a747b920c4",
                                                "text": "Life and death appeared to me ideal bounds, which I should first break through, and pour a torrent of light into our dark world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6413416-ea21-404a-9afa-0f1b4e95d844",
                                                "sense_id": "db4a3c32-86ce-356f-9d1b-97a747b920c4",
                                                "text": "At first, he began to doubt the reality of his adventures, but the acute pain in his shoulders when he attempted to rise, assured him that the kicking of the goblins was certainly not ideal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1bf3a928-3401-33ba-bc34-00361de2167d",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Optimal; being the best possibility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7e4c8ef-a6f0-30a1-9ec3-ccaaafc4e42c",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Perfect, flawless, having no defects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbf2fb60-bdd3-49ca-87dc-560e4e0b5fc9",
                                                "sense_id": "f7e4c8ef-a6f0-30a1-9ec3-ccaaafc4e42c",
                                                "text": "1751 April 13, Samuel Johnson, The Rambler, Number 112, reprinted in 1825, The Works of Samuel Johnson, LL. D., Volume 1, Jones & Company, page 194,\nThere will always be a wide interval between practical and ideal excellence; […] ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1bc1ecd-2cd3-3f17-83f8-15fe8dcbffa6",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Teaching or relating to the doctrine of idealism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23329ded-9c6e-4c00-bb8a-906e0034f6cd",
                                                "sense_id": "b1bc1ecd-2cd3-3f17-83f8-15fe8dcbffa6",
                                                "text": "the ideal theory or philosophy"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c14f0a1-6cf1-339a-8144-6863b18afe73",
                                        "entry_id": "93367181-b405-34cb-b124-7806430bc580",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not actually present, but considered as present when limits at infinity are included."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f87f743b-4085-45b7-a068-788bca5bf348",
                                                "sense_id": "0c14f0a1-6cf1-339a-8144-6863b18afe73",
                                                "text": "ideal point"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72e2ad87-f300-4a03-b347-1382f7968b94",
                                                "sense_id": "0c14f0a1-6cf1-339a-8144-6863b18afe73",
                                                "text": "An ideal triangle in the hyperbolic disk is one bounded by three geodesics that meet precisely on the circle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ideal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "430e0c43-0796-3eb5-8f9f-451cdddf4e51",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A perfect standard of beauty, intellect etc., or a standard of excellence to aim at."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33e1ca6f-4305-40bd-ab3e-64ec65b2c8c3",
                                                "sense_id": "430e0c43-0796-3eb5-8f9f-451cdddf4e51",
                                                "text": "Ideals are like stars; you will not succeed in touching them with your hands. But like the seafaring man on the desert of waters, you choose them as your guides, and following them you will reach your destiny - Carl Schurz"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d10c4f53-7ad0-4947-9a47-b1a551da458c",
                                                "sense_id": "430e0c43-0796-3eb5-8f9f-451cdddf4e51",
                                                "text": "With great humility, I call upon all Americans to help me keep our nation united in defense of those ideals which have been so eloquently proclaimed by Franklin Roosevelt. I want in turn to assure my fellow Americans and all of those who love peace and liberty throughout the world that I will support and defend those ideals with all my strength and all my heart."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A two-sided ideal; a subset of a ring which is closed under both left and right multiplication by elements of the ring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0766e985-2b8a-46b0-a548-34e367c869b6",
                                                "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                                "text": "Let #92;mathbb#123;Z#125; be the ring of integers and let 2#92;mathbb#123;Z#125; be its ideal of even integers. Then the quotient ring #92;mathbb#123;Z#125;#47;2#92;mathbb#123;Z#125; is a Boolean ring."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f63b787a-21e6-4356-8d9c-1486f0827eae",
                                                "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                                "text": "The product of two ideals #92;mathfrak#123;a#125; and #92;mathfrak#123;b#125; is an ideal #92;mathfrak#123;ab#125; which is a subset of the intersection of #92;mathfrak#123;a#125; and #92;mathfrak#123;b#125;. This should help to understand why maximal ideals are prime ideals. Likewise, the union of #92;mathfrak#123;a#125; and #92;mathfrak#123;b#125; is a subset of #92;mathfrak#123;a#43;b#125;."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84143e60-dcd3-41d7-b512-60172afc0b93",
                                                "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                                "text": "In trying to understand the ideal theory of a commutative ring, one quickly sees that it is important to first understand the prime ideals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da4fdff5-b676-4b4d-9fdc-ab6d20172017",
                                                "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                                "text": "If an ideal I of a ring contains the multiplicative identity 1, then we have seen that I must be the entire ring."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74616cd0-0352-4bb5-8bb5-3fbcacddc81f",
                                                "sense_id": "fd12f001-fa04-344b-8d36-e758c9849ee3",
                                                "text": "However, every R has a minimal prime ideal consisting of left zero-divisors and one of right zero-divisors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f5c24fd-a686-33f7-b1b4-a992af72e506",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-empty lower set (of a partially ordered set) which is closed under binary suprema (a.k.a. joins)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d0a7943-01fb-4339-a79a-a392ecef5930",
                                                "sense_id": "0f5c24fd-a686-33f7-b1b4-a992af72e506",
                                                "text": "1992, Unnamed translator, T. S. Fofanova, General Theory of Lattices, in Ordered Sets and Lattices II, American Mathematical Society, page 119,\nAn ideal A of L is called complete if it contains all least upper bounds of its subsets that exist in L. Bishop and Schreiner [80] studied conditions under which joins of ideals in the lattices of all ideals and of all complete ideals coincide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdc9a389-1fe5-45ce-9e75-ec2bc30d8015",
                                                "sense_id": "0f5c24fd-a686-33f7-b1b4-a992af72e506",
                                                "text": "1.35 Find a distributive lattice L with no minimal and no maximal prime ideals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e37df53-1d8f-45e0-af93-5e73aeca118e",
                                                "sense_id": "0f5c24fd-a686-33f7-b1b4-a992af72e506",
                                                "text": "Definition 15.11 (Width Ideal) An ideal Q of a poset P = (X,≤) is a width ideal if maximal(Q) is a width antichain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a00c22eb-27db-392d-bf8f-6eae54d305e1",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of sets, considered small or negligible, such that every subset of each member and the union of any two members are also members of the collection."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aafed00f-15c7-41d9-950b-615000fc8d1c",
                                                "sense_id": "a00c22eb-27db-392d-bf8f-6eae54d305e1",
                                                "text": "Formally, an ideal I of a given set X is a nonempty subset of the powerset #92;mathcal#123;P#125;(X) such that: (1)#92;#92;emptyset#92;inI, (2)#92;A#92;inI#92;andB#92;subseteqA#92;impliesB#92;inI and (3)#92;A,B#92;inI#92;impliesA#92;cupB#92;inI."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09e83497-7fa8-3d0d-b038-624a779c3447",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Lie subalgebra (subspace that is closed under the Lie bracket) 𝖍 of a given Lie algebra 𝖌 such that the Lie bracket [𝖌,𝖍] is a subset of 𝖍."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc910fe5-4a17-43a6-831c-9084988c1210",
                                                "sense_id": "09e83497-7fa8-3d0d-b038-624a779c3447",
                                                "text": "If 𝖌 is a Lie algebra, 𝖍 is an ideal and the Lie algebras 𝖍 and 𝖌/𝖍 are solvable, then 𝖌 is solvable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1039a19-ba46-4f5e-977a-0efa500d1aaf",
                                                "sense_id": "09e83497-7fa8-3d0d-b038-624a779c3447",
                                                "text": "What really put primitive ideals in enveloping algebras of semisimple Lie algebras on the map was Duflo's fundamental theorem that any such ideal is the annihilator of a very special kind of simple module, namely a highest weight module."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62b8c511-77ab-44a4-9811-27310e497c24",
                                                "sense_id": "09e83497-7fa8-3d0d-b038-624a779c3447",
                                                "text": "Next let L be an arbitrary semisimple Lie algebra. Then L can be written uniquely as a direct sum L#95;1#92;oplus#92;dots#92;oplusL#95;t of simple ideals (Theorem 5.2)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "399c1200-623b-394d-ae5d-a93f26e2f754",
                                        "entry_id": "e0fd3eb5-9fc4-3a90-b1f6-59694e4c59ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A subsemigroup with the property that if any semigroup element outside of it is added to any one of its members, the result must lie outside of it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53ee415f-bf7d-49cf-9800-8ef16172e457",
                                                "sense_id": "399c1200-623b-394d-ae5d-a93f26e2f754",
                                                "text": "The set of natural numbers with multiplication as the monoid operation (instead of addition) has multiplicative ideals, such as, for example, the set {1, 3, 9, 27, 81, ...}. If any member of it is multiplied by a number which is not a power of 3 then the result will not be a power of three."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc39c12a-082e-4051-b503-1a908511d380",
                        "source_entry_id": "38f053e3-9424-36e2-bc18-0f1a8f6d908c",
                        "target_lang_word": "idéel",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "idéel",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46328f7c-ad45-3679-b1f2-ac47772a1e75",
                                        "entry_id": "3fc23fee-7679-3684-8125-6bed81150401",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif aux idées, qui a la nature des idées."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31ac94ed-df98-4cd4-beab-2a7bcef039e7",
                                                "sense_id": "46328f7c-ad45-3679-b1f2-ac47772a1e75",
                                                "text": "Peut-être faudrait-il admettre dans notre langue le mot idéel, pour laisser au mot idéal sa signification spéciale. L’idéel est le réel intellectuel, par exemple, nos propriétés, nos facultés morales ; l’idéal est une combinaison résultant de l’action de l’idéel, ou une vue, une perception de l’idéel dans son type. Lorsque la forme ou le sentiment de l’idéal est passé en nous par la perception, il devient idéel, partie de nous-mêmes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd8024e-fce3-4f80-8442-551cdcc3d606",
                                                "sense_id": "46328f7c-ad45-3679-b1f2-ac47772a1e75",
                                                "text": "Constatons-le, c’est sur la physique que se termine ce paragraphe qui décrit donc un va-et-vient enrichissant entre expérience et concepts : les concepts fondamentaux ne sont pas là dès le début, mais, dès le stade de la description, il y a des cadres idéels vagues […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fcfd97f-060f-4061-ade2-04ad6db73f15",
                                                "sense_id": "46328f7c-ad45-3679-b1f2-ac47772a1e75",
                                                "text": "Vus d’en bas, les rayons où perlent encore des gouttes s’étoilent contre le ciel en une rosace immaculée, je pourrais presque dire idéelle si je ne la voyais si proche de moi, quoique sans poids, sans substance apparente et pourtant présente, frémissante, inamovible entre ses points d’attache avec ce cœur immobile au centre des rayons, pattes tendues sur les fils frissonnants. […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
